.TH AVR\-GROUP\-CREATE 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-create \- Create a group below a parent group.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group create
[OPTIONS] NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a group below a parent group.
.PP
NAME is the new group's name, unique below its parent. --parent names the parent like GROUP in other group commands; the root group, Organization unless renamed, takes groups at the top of the tree.
.PP
Each create sends an idempotency key, printed to standard error before the request. If the response is lost, rerun the same command with --idempotency-key KEY: it returns the group that create made instead of making a second one. A key belongs to one parent, name and label.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr group create Platform --parent Organization
    avr group create CI --parent Organization/Platform --label runners
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    created_at, display_name, group_id, idempotency_key, label, member_count,
    ownership, parent_id, soft_deleted_at, state, suspension_reason,
    updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fINAME\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-parent\fR \fITEXT\fR
The group to create it below. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fITEXT\fR
A short label shown with the group.
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fIUUID\fR
Resume an earlier create with the key it printed.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
